> - 6 October 2026 : WHY THE CYCLES VIEW LOOKED UGLY AND HOW IT WAS FIXED. (a) Cycles reads the material PREVIEW network (`UsdPreviewSurface`), not the Karma Principled shader. The preview normal map, read the wrong way, drew black fibres on the petals and black patches on the leaves: a Python LOP `lt_cycles_preview_fix` (placed after `lt_assign`, before `lt_camera`) clears the `inputs:normal` connection of every UsdPreviewSurface; Karma keeps its own normal map. (b) Lights: Cycles is much more sensitive than Karma and the dome is the VISIBLE background, so the dome sets the background grey: dome intensity 0.25 and exposure -1.3 gives a mid grey; key light exposure -0.8 with angle 6 (soft shadows); a FILL light `lt_fill` (copy of the key, rotation y + 160, x -15, exposure -1.9) lights the sides in shadow. Karma values to restore for Karma: dome 1.0 / 0, key 1.5. (20 October 2026, 13:47:50 +0200)
